<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #1: off, both arms of the match spell the Result payload by offset" min="2" max="2">v2\.payload\.field_0x8</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #2: on, the guarded arm names Ok, which is the variant DW_AT_discr_value 0 selects" min="1" max="1">v1 = v2\.payload\.Ok;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #3: on, the arm rustc hoisted above the branch names Err, reached through the def-use walk" min="1" max="1">\(int8\)v2\.payload\.Err \+ 100</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #4: Ok and Err are never both written on one arm, so the two arms cannot be swapped" min="0" max="0">payload\.Ok \+ 100</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #5: a branchless discriminant is not a seed, so put_res keeps the offset spelling in BOTH passes" min="2" max="2">\(dst-&gt;payload\)\.field_0x8\.__0 = v1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #6: an Option already names its only payload variant, so the layout is skipped in BOTH passes" min="2" max="2">\(dst-&gt;payload\)\.Some\.__0 =</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #7: off, a literal-tag constructor still spells both overlaying facets by offset" min="1" max="1">\(rethidden-&gt;payload\)\.field_0x4\.a = x;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #8: on, the constant store over the tag names the variant it builds" min="1" max="1">\(rethidden-&gt;payload\)\.P\.a = x;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #9: on, and so does the other arm, which stores discriminant 1" min="1" max="1">\(rethidden-&gt;payload\)\.Q\.field_0x8 = \(uint8\)x;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARIANTGUARD #10: disjoint payload ranges are already forced by the layout, so ret_three is identical in BOTH passes" min="2" max="2">\(rethidden-&gt;payload\)\.A\.__0 = x;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
